# Unused lambda parameters → `_`

When a lambda parameter is unused in the body, declare it as the Java unnamed variable `_`
(JDK 22+; Ezkey uses JDK 25).

```java
// Bad — unused named parameter (Checkstyle: UnusedLambdaParameterShouldBeUnnamed)
(root, query, cb) -> cb.equal(root.get("id"), id)
cache.get(key, k -> new Bucket())

// Good
(root, _, cb) -> cb.equal(root.get("id"), id)
cache.get(key, _ -> new Bucket())
```

Enforced by Checkstyle module `UnusedLambdaParameterShouldBeUnnamed` in
`checkstyle-config/src/main/resources/checkstyle.xml`. Do not suppress routinely; rename instead.
